6,Mambila Studies,https://mambila.info/,"The Virtual Institute of Mambila Studies seeks to collate and connect the different research and researchers with an interest in the Mambila people of the Nigeria - Cameroon borderland and their neighbours; their languages and the area in which they live. We take a broad view of Mambila, including other groups speaking related languages such as Kwanja, Vute, Wawa, Nizaa, Njerep (3 speakers at ...","Mambila, Nigeria",Niger-Congo
7,Mambila - Song by World Music Atelier - Apple Music,https://music.apple.com/ng/song/mambila/453201714,Listen to Mambila by World Music Atelier on Apple Music. 2011. Duration: 3:06,"Mambila, Nigeria",Niger-Congo
8,Mambila - Hartenberger World Musical Instrument Collection,https://wmic.net/african-cultures/mambila-2/,"The preferred ethnonym is spelt Mambila in Cameroon and Mambilla in Nigeria. ""Norr"" is also used (the word for person in Nigerian dialects of Mambilla). The Mambila people produced a considerable number of masks and figures that are characterized by a heart-shaped face; red and white pigments were often applied later.","Mambila, Nigeria",Niger-Congo
9,Mambiloid languages,https://grokipedia.com/page/mambiloid_languages,"The Mambiloid languages constitute a branch of the Niger-Congo language family, specifically within the Atlantic-Congo subgroup and classified under Northern Bantoid. They are spoken primarily along the Nigeria-Cameroon border region, encompassing the Adamawa Plateau and surrounding areas in eastern Nigeria (such as Taraba State) and northern Cameroon (including the Mambila Plateau). This ...","Mambila, Nigeria",Niger-Congo
